  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The leaf shape and color set this cultivar apart, as does the delightful green bark with a faint whitish dusting and distinct white striations. Fall color is one of the best bright yellow-golds of the green dissectums. The medium-sized deep green leaves have five to seven lobes which are deeply but not finely cut to the midrib. The lobes look more feathery, while most green dissectums look lacier. 'Sekimori' is a strong, hardy plant, reaching 10-13 ft. (3-4 m) high and 13-16 ft. (4-5 m) wide. Planting it on a Vertrees. slope enhances its beauty. Oddly, the name means \"a border guard post. \""
  },
